{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>From men</b> — Joined to the verse above; the meaning is, deliver me by Your hand from men who are Your plague, for it is in [Your] hand, as: הנה יד ה' הויה (behold, the hand of YHWH came to pass)." "<b>From men of the world</b> — For all their desire is to be among the dwellers of this world, for חלד is not a lasting thing; the witness is וחלדי כאין נגדך כל יושבי חלד. And all their request is to live many years, and every hidden good that You have is to fill their belly in this world and delight in it. They rejoice and are sated; they leave what remains for their children's offspring."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:29.124110902Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}